rcq("R02-C-08-4", "Application / analogy", "Difficult",
    "Which of the following is most closely analogous to what happens, on the account the author favours, when mental fatigue sets in?",
    "A shopper who has spent an hour in one store grows restless as the other stores nearby seem ever more worth the time.",
    [("A car slows to a halt on the motorway because the petrol in its tank has finally run out after a long journey.",
      "This is the fuel-gauge picture of paragraph 1, the model that paragraph 2 says has 'fared badly', not the account the author favours."),
     ("A runner's leg muscles weaken over the course of a long race and need several days of rest before regaining strength.",
      "This depicts a store used up by effort and restored by rest, which is the resource model rather than a shift in what one is 'willing to pay for'."),
     ("A student stops revising for an examination because she has now covered everything that the syllabus requires.",
      "Stopping because a task is complete involves no rising opportunity cost; the author's account concerns weariness while the task is unfinished.")],
    "Paragraph 3 says continued effort 'carries an opportunity cost, the value of everything else one might be doing instead', and weariness rises as that cost accumulates. The shopper's restlessness grows as alternatives look more valuable, not because anything has run out.",
    "Choosing the runner, which looks like the everyday experience of tiredness but mirrors the depletion model.",
    "Two distractors model the rejected theory in concrete form; the student must map the structure of the favoured account, not the surface experience of tiredness.",
    cognitive="Application", exams=DX)

